       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the safe maximum and may be a transcription error.\n\n**Why the dose is too high:**\n- **Per dose:** The usual maximum single oral dose of ibuprofen is 800 mg. The order is for 1600 mg.\n- **Per day:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6400 mg/day. The prescription maximum is 3200 mg/day, so this is twice that. Doses this high carry a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury and other toxicity, even in a patient with normal organ function.\n\n**Possible intended orders:**\n1. **400 mg four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). This is a common analgesic regimen.\n2. **800 mg three times daily** (2400 mg/day), or **800 mg four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum) for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n3. Something else you had in mind.\n\nTell me the correct dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. If 1600 mg per dose really is intended, for example under a specialist protocol, please confirm that and give the reason. I'll add it as a note on the order, but it should go to pharmacy for review before it's given."
