       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. I know you've confirmed it, and I realise this holds up your workflow.\n\nFor a 70 kg adult, 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day. That's twice the 3200 mg/day prescription maximum and twice the 800 mg maximum single dose. I don't know of any oral ibuprofen protocol for adults that uses this regimen. Even the high-dose protocol for cystic fibrosis is given twice daily and adjusted to blood levels. At this dose, the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis and CNS toxicity is high. Without a specific clinical reason, I can't treat this as an intentional order.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n- Enter **800 mg four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum) or **800 mg three times daily** (2400 mg/day)\n- Enter **400 mg four times daily** (1600 mg/day), in case \"1600\" was meant as the total daily dose\n- Enter a different dose you choose, as long as it's within the standard range\n\n**If you really need this dose:** tell me the indication or the protocol it comes from. With that, I can enter the order with a note that sends it to pharmacy for review before it's given. You could also place it directly with a pharmacist or through your system's override process, so someone with full clinical context can sign off on it.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
